[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form: \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then, we can substitute \(z\) into the expression and simplify.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m First, let's express \(z\) and \(\frac{1}{z}\) in terms of \(\theta\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[z = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m Now, substitute these into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[(75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + (96 + 144i)\frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)\]
