[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of trigonometric identities. The expression \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\) can be written as \(R \cos(\theta + \phi)\), where \(R = \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\) and \(\tan \phi = \frac{432}{324} = \frac{4}{3}\).
