[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m [response] To find the largest possible real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\), we can use the properties of complex numbers and their magnitudes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m Let \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m (75 + 117i)(4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m First, we simplify the terms:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m (75 + 117i)(4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4} = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m Combining these, the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + (24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m = (4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m = (300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m = (324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta) + i(324\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). To find the maximum value of this expression, we can use the method of finding the amplitude of the sinusoidal function. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:
