[36m(TaskRunner pid=10888)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\). To find the maximum value of this expression, we can use the method of finding the amplitude of a sinusoidal function. The maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:
